Body:
> Any movement on this? Claude just launched sub-agents within sub-agents (5 levels deep), even just having 2 levels deep would be great.

@sboisvert I've been using this PR daily since I made it.   It's working, stable code, though I haven't rebased my OpenCode build from upstream in over a month. I remain committed to my development roadmap for the Agentic Collaboration Framework in which this PR is one component of many.  I view my work at this point as creating the critical infrastructure for complex multi agent orchestration in OpenCode. As maintainers showed no interest in this PR, and haven't produced an equivalent or better feature change for upstream, I've been keeping what I've been building private. I suppose I could be ready to publish in a few weeks. But it feels like a waste of time trying to submit PRs to OpenCode at this point and the drama of publishing an OpenCode fork that usurps upstream seems like it could become an unwanted distraction from my main objective which is to use my Harness and the tools I've developed for civil rights litigation. 

I had hoped to submit what I built and have it merged. The idea of becoming a developer who maintains a competing project is very unappealing to me

**Update:** as of 1.17.5 this is no longer necessary; it can be toggled in the UI. See my comment below: https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/30360#issuecomment-4699682022

Original: For people using `opencode web` or `opencode serve` (and may also work on desktop app, but I haven't tested), you can run this snippet in the devtools console to set the `settings.general.showCustomAgents` internal setting to `true`:
```js
const s = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('settings.v3') || '{}');
s.general = s.general || {};
s.general.showCustomAgents = true;
localStorage.setItem('settings.v3', JSON.stringify(s));
location.reload();
```

**Also reproduced from agent-shell (Emacs ACP client) on v1.15.0.**

Third independent client hitting this. Setup: [agent-shell](https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell) (Emacs) spawning `opencode acp` over stdio, with a custom OpenAI-compatible provider (`@ai-sdk/openai-compatible`) pointing at a self-hosted Open WebUI instance, model `nemotron-3-super:120b` (long streamed replies, which seems to widen the race window).

A `session/update` with an `agent_message_chunk` arrived after the `session/prompt` response had already closed the turn — agent-shell flags the protocol violation explicitly. The late chunk is a fragment of the final message text, so the visible symptom is the tail of the assistant's reply going missing in the client.

Late notification payload:

```json
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "method": "session/update",
  "params": {
    "sessionId": "ses_143854e16ffet8E0j59kYRgaFW",
    "update": {
      "sessionUpdate": "agent_message_chunk",
      "messageId": "msg_ebce90c09001gryYsSnuDhEeCe",
      "content": {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "EM"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Matches the spec ordering requirement cited in the issue description: all `session/update` notifications must be written before the `session/prompt` response.
